.th TTYS V 8/12/77
.sh NAME
ttys - typewriter initialization data
.sh DESCRIPTION
The format of the
.it ttys
file is as described in The Book.

The third character in each line identifies
the type of terminal.
Current types at the University of Wollongong are:
.in +10
.ta 4
.nf
-	Carousel: 300 baud
0	Local VDU: 300 baud
2	Local VDU: 1200 baud
4	Local VDU: 2400 baud
5	Local VDU: 4800 baud
.in -10
.fi
.sh FILES
/etc/ttys
.sh "SEE ALSO"
The Book
